### Code Smell API — local requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Start the server first:  ./run.sh        (http://localhost:8080)
### Each request sends a fixture file as the raw text/plain body.
### When an API key is configured, add:  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Clean code -> 200 []  (no smells)
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

< src/test/resources/smells/CleanCode.java

### Dead Code -> UnusedLocalVariable
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

< src/test/resources/smells/DeadCode.java

### Global Mutable State -> MutableStaticState
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

< src/test/resources/smells/GlobalMutableState.java

### Magic Number -> AvoidLiteralsInIfCondition
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

< src/test/resources/smells/MagicNumber.java

### Nested If Canyon -> AvoidDeeplyNestedIfStmts
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

< src/test/resources/smells/NestedIfCanyon.java

### Primitive Obsession -> UseObjectForClearerAPI
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

< src/test/resources/smells/PrimitiveObsession.java

### Swallowed Exception -> EmptyCatchBlock
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

< src/test/resources/smells/SwallowedException.java

### Empty body -> 400 (code is required)
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

### Unparseable code -> 400 (code could not be parsed)
POST {{host}}/analyze
Content-Type: text/plain

